        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Reporters Committee for Freedom of the Press, CBS News\n- People: Walter Cronkite, Wolf Blitzer, Tony Mauro, Andrea Mitchell, Judy Woodruff, Kathy Cronkite\n- Roles: steering committee members, anchorman, broadcast journalist\n\nFacts:\n- Walter Cronkite was born on November 4, 1916, and died on July 17, 2009.\n- Walter Cronkite was an American broadcast journalist.\n- Walter Cronkite was the anchorman of the CBS Evening News for 19 years from 1962 to 1981.\n- Walter Cronkite was an active member of the Reporters Committee for Freedom of the Press from 1973 until his death in 2009.\n- The steering committee of the Reporters Committee for Freedom of the Press includes Wolf Blitzer, Tony Mauro, Andrea Mitchell, and Judy Woodruff.\n- Kathy Cronkite is a daughter of former CBS News anchorman Walter Cronkite.",
